### ============================================================================
### !! SUPERSEDED AS A DESCRIPTION OF THE BENCH -- 2026-09-01.
###    This file is NOT the tb470 bench's state and must not be read as it. It is a
###    purpose-built, single-DUT rig for the 5700 bootloader campaign of 2026-08-11,
###    when the two IE520s were STANDALONE and each was bound as swi_a in its own run.
###    They have been ONE STACK since 2026-08-18, so this file's device roles, hub
###    links and portlinks no longer describe anything that is cabled.
###    Current bench state: ~/claude/IE520-testing/bench-setup/bench-state.md
###    (from which /home/st-art/st-art/configs/tb470.setup is generated).
###    Kept because it is the record of how that campaign was rigged, and because its
###    portlink notes are the independent 2026-08-11 corroboration of which LAG leg
###    lands on which AR4050S port -- cited in the bench-state record.
### ============================================================================
### tb470 - IE520 on /dev/u4, bound as role swi_a.  Run A (suite 2002).
### Management port cabled to tb470 eth3.  PDU socket labelled "D".
###
### Derived from the tb504 5700 default.setup, with three deliberate differences.
### Read the notes before changing anything here.
###
###  1. BAUD IS 115200, not 9600.  Both tb470 IE520s are silent at 9600 and clean
###     at 115200 (probed 2026-08-11).  AWPConsoleCore._connect_serial() opens the
###     port ONCE at this rate and never renegotiates, so this value serves both
###     the bootloader and the AW+ CLI.
###
###  2. There are TWO links here and they do different jobs.  I originally declared
###     only the hub link, reasoning that the scripts use dut.portA / tb.ethA merely
###     as a fallback and in two log lines.  That was WRONG, and a 2026-08-11 smoke
###     run proved it: ATTools.download_file_from_tftp() resolves the link ITSELF via
###     setup.get_all_port_links(swi, tb), independent of the script, and with none
###     declared it fell back to the hub link and tried to configure `eth0` from the
###     AW+ CLI -- an interface that only exists in the bootloader.  Result:
###     "Unable to ping TFTP server 10.38.215.65", flash never populated.
###       hub link   = BOOTLOADER TFTP boot, over the USB dongle (eth0).
###       tb-swi_a   = POST-BOOTUP CLI file transfer, over a real front-panel port.
###     The second is also how the port gets ENABLED at all: the framework's generated
###     default.cfg does `int port1.0.1-port1.0.28 / shutdown`, and only the declared
###     portlink port is brought back up (portA.up() / `no shutdown`).
###
###  3. This DUT has eth3 to itself, and the u5 run has eth2 - one wire each, no
###     shared segment.  KEEP eth3 DEDICATED TO THIS DUT.  The bootloader address is
###     derived from the tty number - library_5700.py:159
###         ipDevice = tb_eth_a.get_ipv4_addr(2 + int(dut.ttyNumber))
###     so /dev/u4 on eth3 (10.38.215.64/27) resolves to 10.38.215.70 - which is
###     INSIDE dhcpd's pool for that subnet (range 10.38.215.68 - 10.38.215.94, and
###     dhcpd is bound to eth3).  Nothing else can claim .70 while the wire is
###     point-to-point, but note that dhcpd's ping-check cannot protect an address
###     whose owner is switched off, and 2002 powers this DUT off about 24 times.
###     If anything else is ever put on eth3, exclude .68-.71 from that pool first.

[power]
### Front-panel "D" = outlet 4.  The outlet field is NUMERIC - Setup.py:588 does
### int(outTuple[2]) for any non-'awplus' type, so the faceplate letter raises.
### The mapping is A-H = 1-8, from SESSION_STATE.md 2026-07-30: this same PDU has
### the AR4050S on outlet 8 ("H") and the x230 on outlet 6 ("F").
pwr_a = (pdu, 10.36.150.14, 4)

[switch]
swi_a = /dev/u4

[baudrates]
swi_a = 115200

[powerlink]
swi_a = pwr_a

### Device TFTP boots over its management port ###
[hub]
hub_a = tb, swi_a

[portlink]
### BOOTLOADER TFTP boot link: tb470 eth3 (10.38.215.65/27) <-> the IE520's USB
### ethernet dongle, which the bootloader calls eth0.  DUT boots at 10.38.215.70,
### TFTP server is eth3's own 10.38.215.65.  The dongle shares the switch's single
### rear USB port via a hub, alongside the USB boot-media options.
hub_a-tb = eth3
hub_a-swi_a = eth0

### POST-BOOTUP CLI file-transfer link -- this is what populates flash with
### mainrelease.rel / backuprelease.rel, and what 2002 case 30 uses to copy a
### wrong-platform release.  NOT a direct cable:
###     swi_a port1.0.1 -> AR4050S (swi_c) port1.0.3 -> vlan1 -> AR4050S uplink
###                     -> tb470 eth1 10.38.215.1/27
### An intermediate switch is fine because the framework makes the DUT port an
### UNTAGGED access port in a fresh VLAN and statically addresses it in eth1's
### subnet (ipOffset = ttyNumber + 2, so /dev/u4 -> 10.38.215.6), then pings
### 10.38.215.1.  It needs one L2 broadcast domain and NO routed hop -- there is no
### default route on the DUT.  Verified 2026-08-11: all 8 AR4050S ports are untagged
### members of vlan1, and tb470 eth1 pings the AR4050S vlan1 (10.38.215.3) 0% loss.
###
### !! Do NOT re-route this through swi_b. Each run's default.cfg shuts EVERY port on
### !! its own DUT, so the two IE520s must not depend on one another.
###
### NOTE: .6 (and .7 for the u5 run) sit inside dhcpd's eth1 pool .2-.10. Only a risk
### while the DUT is powered off -- which these suites do constantly.
tb-swi_a = eth1-port1.0.1
